    "text": "Mecklenburg County, North Carolina\nWho is and isn't backing the roads/transit tax\nBy WFAE,\n11 hours agoMecklenburg County voters will decide in November whether to increase the sales tax by one cent, to 8.25%, to pay for a multibillion-dollar roads and transit plan. With three months until the referendum, the tax has so far produced some unusual political alliances. WFAE Morning Edition host Marshall Terry spoke...",
